},{"text":"and reacting to it in that the cancellation handler is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"always"}]},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"immediately","type":"text"}]},{"text":" invoked when the task is canceled. For example, even if the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operation is running code that never checks for cancellation, a cancellation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"handler still runs and provides a chance to run some cleanup code:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["await withTaskCancellationHandler {","  var sum = 0","  while condition {","    sum += 1","  }","  return sum","} onCancel: {","  \/\/ This onCancel closure might execute concurrently with the operation.","  condition.cancel()","}"]},{"text":"Execution order and semantics","anchor":"Execution-order-and-semantics","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operation"},{"text":" closure is always invoked, even when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler(operation:onCancel:)"},{"text":" method is called from a task","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that was already canceled.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler(operation:onCancel:)"},{"text":" is used in a task that has already been","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"canceled, the cancellation handler will be executed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"immediately before the ","type":"text"},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure gets to execute.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This allows the cancellation handler to 